  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070279",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-96948",
      "knowledge_point_id": "8742ad90-1d33-5b56-a83f-8edd7f2f5aef",
      "knowledge_point": "Using a Percentage Points Table and Symmetry To Find the Z-Score for a Given Probability",
      "problem": "The table below gives the values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z>z)=0.30.$\n\n| $\\,p\\,$ | $0.55$ | $0.60$ | $0.65$ | $0.70$ | $0.75$ | $0.80$ | $0.85$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,0.1257\\,$ | $\\,0.2533\\,$ | $\\,0.3853\\,$ | $\\,0.5244\\,$ | $\\,0.6745\\,$ | $\\,0.8416\\,$ | $\\,1.0364\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "First, we express the given information in terms of $Φ,$ using the complement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z>z) & =0.30 \\\\ 1-P(Z\\le z) & =0.30 \\\\ 1-Φ(z) & =0.30 \\\\ Φ(z) & =1-0.30 \\\\ Φ(z) & =0.70\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we are looking for the value of $z$ such that\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.70).\n$$\n\nWe look for the column in the table that corresponds to $p=0.70,$ and we find that\n\n$$\np=0.70\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(p)=0.5244.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.70)=0.5244.\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
